## Notes for the reviewer

- The writer had no shell; every selector and timing comes from reading `src/runtime/layer.ts`, `scheduler.ts`, `main.ts`, `CommandDock.ts`, `BuildWindow.ts` and `focus-rule.ts`.
- Clocked tests click page controls with `element.click()` in `page.evaluate` (Playwright's click waits for animation frames, which the fake clock freezes); window bar clicks use `page.mouse.click`, which does not. Keyboard input uses `page.keyboard.press`.
- Sampled moments: idle thresholds are sampled at 3 s and 4.5 s (4 s threshold, 500 ms margin); the done collapse at 2 s and 5 s; turbo and 1x durations carry 150 to 300 ms tolerances (progress rounds to 1 %, 20 ms steps). The 2x hero check accepts 1100 to 2100 ms because the boot runs a few frames in real time before the clock pauses; 1x would exceed 2400 ms.
- The deep-link hero check is an upper bound only (a fifth of 3100 ms plus 250 ms), since the hero may run a few frames at 1x before the deep link queues it.
- Stack renders no focusable element, so the Stack focus test adds `tabindex="0"` to its heading; the ring check uses a Projects card link.
- Shift + Esc in a real Chrome for Windows window is not claimed here (owner step).

